7.1 Authentication API — /api/auth/
 POST   /api/auth/register/
Register a new account
Auth required: None
Creates a new user with role "user" (the admin role cannot be self-assigned). Passwords are validated for strength and the email must not already exist.
Request Body:
Field	Type	Description
email	string	Required, must be unique
password	string	Required, must meet password strength rules
full_name	string	Required
phone_number	string	Optional; Kenyan format (07XXXXXXXX or +2547XXXXXXXX)
Example Response:
{
  "id": "b3f1...uuid",
  "email": "jane@example.com",
  "full_name": "Jane Wanjiru",
  "phone_number": "0712345678",
  "role": "user"
}

 POST   /api/auth/login/
Log in and receive tokens
Auth required: None
Validates credentials and, on success, returns a JWT access/refresh token pair plus the authenticated user's profile. Fails with 401 for invalid credentials or a deactivated account.
Request Body:
Field	Type	Description
email	string	Required
password	string	Required
Example Response:
{
  "message": "Login successful",
  "access_token": "eyJhbGciOi...",
  "refresh_token": "eyJhbGciOi...",
  "user": { "id": "...", "email": "jane@example.com", "role": "user", ... }
}

 POST   /api/auth/logout/
Log out (blacklist refresh token)
Auth required: Required
Blacklists the supplied refresh token so it can no longer be exchanged for a new access token. Always returns success even if the token was already invalid, to avoid leaking token validity.
Request Body:
Field	Type	Description
refresh_token	string	The refresh token to invalidate
Example Response:
{
  "message": "Logout successful"
}

 POST   /api/auth/refresh/
Refresh an access token
Auth required: None (refresh token acts as the credential)
Standard SimpleJWT TokenRefreshView. Exchanges a valid, non-expired refresh token for a new access token.
Request Body:
Field	Type	Description
refresh	string	A valid refresh token
Example Response:
{
  "access": "eyJhbGciOi..."
}

 GET   /api/auth/me/
Get the current user's profile
Auth required: Required
Returns the authenticated user's own profile.
Example Response:
{
  "id": "...", "email": "jane@example.com", "full_name": "Jane Wanjiru",
